      "problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =4\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}+C \\\\  & =2{ln}^{2}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
